RECORDED AS AN IDEA (@ajs, 2026-10-18: "Record h, i and j as ideas").

FROM REA (clone at /home/ajs7/project/rea, HEAD 92dadf933): src/domain/residualUnknown.ts. An unknown is revisioned and hash-chained:
- its status is open, investigating, blocked, contradicted or resolved;
- it carries supporting_evidence_ids and contradicting_evidence_ids;
- it says what would settle it: required_authority, required_confidence and recommended_probes;
- a resolution is `verified` (it needs at least one evidence id) or withdrawn or out-of-scope.
REA's skill adds: "Mark each question as answered, partially answered, or unresolved… do not describe a broad investigation as complete while required questions remain open."

THE IDEA FOR REFLOW2: today a Question records whom it was put to and who answered (cap:a-question-names-whom-it-was-put-to-and-who-answered), and a gap names what is missing. Neither says what would SETTLE it. The idea: an open Question or gap may carry what would settle it (the evidence, its required level, a suggested probe or computation), and a "settled by evidence" closure names that evidence. A partially answered state is kept rather than forced to answered or open.

SIZE, as a finding: small (a few optional fields on Question, and the read-back).

NOT CHOSEN; nothing to build.
